==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AuthRequired  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AuthRequired.als
    rationale: removing this fact lets the model build an Operation with opAuthenticated=BoolFalse and opOutcome=Success, which is exactly what the AuthRequired invariant forbids.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CrossTeamIsolation  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_CrossTeamIsolation.als
    rationale: without the cross-team-isolation fact, an Operation can succeed against a task in another team, leaking existence and breaking the byte-equivalent 404 invariant.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_014_CrossTeamByteEquivalent, FR_011_NoCrossTeamRoleAccess
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_014_CrossTeamByteEquivalent: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_NoCrossTeamRoleAccess: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnerOrAdminMutation  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_OwnerOrAdminMutation.als
    rationale: clearing this fact allows a non-owner non-admin member to successfully PATCH or DELETE a task they do not own — the central FR-009 violation.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_009_NonOwnerCannotMutate, FR_008_MemberOwnsCanEdit, LeastPrivilege
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_009_NonOwnerCannotMutate: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_008_MemberOwnsCanEdit: FAIL (expected)
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAppendOnly  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AuditAppendOnly.als
    rationale: removing this fact lets two distinct operations bind to the same AuditEntry, contradicting the append-only one-source-per-entry invariant.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_016_AuditAppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditPerStateChange  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AuditPerStateChange.als
    rationale: removing this fact allows a successful CreateTask (or PatchTask/DeleteTask) with no associated AuditEntry, breaking the per-edit-event audit invariant.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttribution  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AuditAttribution.als
    rationale: removing this fact allows an AuditEntry whose recorded actor differs from the producing operation's caller — misattribution of who did what.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_015_AuditSnapshot
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_AuditSnapshot: FAIL (expected)

